VARIETY AND FRESHNESS RULES:

🚫 BANNED OPENING PATTERNS:
- NEVER start with: "[Subject] is a [adjective] [noun]"
❌ "Istanbul is a big city"
❌ "The Göktürks were a powerful empire"
❌ "This topic is very important"

✅ APPROVED OPENING STRATEGIES:
1. Start with a SPECIFIC FACT:
✓ "In 1453, the Ottoman army crossed the Bosphorus..."
✓ "The first Göktürk inscription dates back to 735 CE..."

2. Start with a QUESTION:
✓ "Have you ever wondered why Istanbul has two continents?"
✓ "What made the Turks migrate westward?"

3. Start with a SENSORY DETAIL:
✓ "The smell of fresh simit fills the morning streets..."
✓ "The sound of drums echoed across the steppe..."

4. Start with a COMPARISON:
✓ "Unlike other ancient cities, Istanbul..."
✓ "While many empires rose and fell, the Turks..."

5. Start with a QUOTE or SAYING:
✓ "As the old saying goes, 'He who controls Istanbul...'"

📏 PARAGRAPH VARIETY:
- First 3 words of consecutive paragraphs MUST be different
- No two paragraphs may start with the same grammatical structure
- Vary sentence length within paragraphs (short-medium-long rhythm)

🔄 CROSS-CONTENT VARIETY:
- No two pieces in the same topic tree may share the same opening sentence
- Sibling topics must use DIFFERENT opening strategies
